        {
          "type": "h2",
          "text": "WHY WE CALL IT SECONDPASSPORT"
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "I finished my BSc at North South University in 2016. A year later I moved to Dublin for a Master's at Trinity College Dublin. That degree changed what I could do with my life. It worked like a second passport."
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Most of the process was guesswork: which university, how much money to show, what the visa officer wanted to see. SecondPassport is the help I wish I had: someone who looks at your real profile and tells you where you can actually get in."
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "We start with the UK and Ireland, where I know the system first hand, and we are adding more countries."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "2017"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Moved from Dhaka to Dublin"
        },
